Topic: Traffic Light System.

Objective: design a system to control traffic lights based on real-time vehicle flow. This system should use data collected from sensors, cameras, and GPS devices to detect traffic density and adjust light timings. In this project, you could use shortest-path algorithms to calculate optimal routes and travel times.
System Architecture will provide:
a) Data layer to extract data from sensors such as a sensor to count vehicles per lane, a sensor to determine density of traffic, or a GPS feed sensor which will take vehicle speed & traffic density to determine adjustments of light signal(timings) changes at the given intersection/ road.
Expectations: 
	Return Vehicle count / time
	Return a lane capacity for given road(if capacity full preempt light change?)
	Return Average speed
	Return a Queue to determine which signal to change based on V.count & congestion(from 	avg speed)
	Possibly keep track on congestion per grid intersection.
	Return current light signals dynamically. 
	Return wait time- per light (per-determined or possibly dynamically)
b) Handle all computations for data from section a. 
c)Algorithms & Data Structures:
	Dynamic Signal timing Algo: instead of using a fixed timer, adjust lights based on traffic density  - High = extend Green, low = extend red/ short green. Implement a max wait time to preempt(no starvation).
	Possible algorithms- Greedy, priority Queue or RR(round robin schedule)
		Pseudo – 
			For (intersection|| edge(road)):
				Compute Traffic density:
				compare(intersections)
				select light
				adjust timing : check density repeat.
	Shortest Path – Algorithms Dijkstra's ? A*? Dynamic Recomputation of shortest paths
	Grid – intersections & roads? Nodes = intersections
Edges = roads
Edge weight = travel time (base time + estimated delay)
Data Structures – Graph, Queues, Adjacency List through a linked list/ Std::Vector<Vector><edges>
